# Hindsight memory — {{BANK_ID}}

This project's default Hindsight bank is `{{BANK_ID}}` (see `.hindsight.json`;
`memory_get_current_bank` lists every bank this project may use). Auto-recall and
auto-retain are off unless `.hindsight.json` turns them on.

## What happens automatically

- **Before each user prompt** — only if `.hindsight.json` sets `autoRecall: true` —
  the recall hook searches the default bank and silently appends relevant
  memories to the message. Claude sees them, the user does not.
- **After each response / on session end** — only if `autoRetain: true`
  (default false) — the retain hooks capture the transcript. Off by default:
  memory is for curated facts and decisions, not raw conversation.

So with the defaults, **write deliberately** with `memory_retain` (pass `bank`
when the fact belongs to a bank other than the default), and recall by hand
when the task needs history.

